    "proof": "At every rank r, choose r independent Boolean generators already contained in L and r coordinate rows with nonzero determinant. The determinantal divisor [Sat(span L):L] divides every full-rank minor, so it is at most the chosen Boolean determinant and hence r^(r/2). A proper same-span extension has integer index at least two and therefore reduces this saturation index by at least two. There are at most k-1 rank increases, yielding L(k). Choose the positions and Boolean identities of the non-self columns with (m+1)^L(2^k+1)^L possibilities. Every self-loop pattern on a path to a bad terminal lattice is contained in that terminal lattice, whose relative Boolean base is at most 1-2^-k. The Smith numerator and fixed register-offset factors are bounded by k^(k/2)2^(kc). Taking logarithms gives the stated condition.",
